# Granot Lifecycle Capture

Owner invariants: [`.cursor/businesslogic/granotLifecycle.capture.md`](../businesslogic/granotLifecycle.capture.md). Decision/activation/Record Link: [`.cursor/businesslogic/granotLifecycle.processor.md`](../businesslogic/granotLifecycle.processor.md). Claim/drainer: [`.cursor/businesslogic/granotLifecycle.drainer.md`](../businesslogic/granotLifecycle.drainer.md).

- `src/services/granotLifecycle/capture.ts` is the only webhook insert path. `granotWebhooks/` is a deprecated adapter.
- Authenticate with `requireGranotWebhookSecret`, persist one credential-redacted v2 receipt, return `202` only after Mongo commit, then optionally publish `{ receipt_id }`.
- Capture still does not normalize or process. `normalization.ts` is a callable Observation module only. `sourcePolicy.ts` is a fail-closed Registry read/gate module. `processor.ts` is a callable Decision/Record Link skeleton only. None of those are invoked from capture. Admin routes activate, requeue dead letters, project a Job, or read health — they do not own claim/match/patch policy.
- `granot-lifecycle-events*` wake-ups are consumed by `api/queues/granot-lifecycle-consumer.ts`, which accepts only `{ receipt_id }` and calls the shared drainer. Five-minute cron `/api/cron/granot-lifecycle-drain` scans due work. Mongo claim/fence selects the single winner. Publish failure must not change `202`.
- Processing disabled means no claim; capture and due work remain intact. Shadow/retry/requeue must not create, update, cancel, or un-cancel a Booking.

Delivery branches: [`lead-lifecycle-delivery.mdc`](lead-lifecycle-delivery.mdc). Locked contracts: `scripts/prototypes/granot-lead-lifecycle/specs/FINAL-SPECIFICATION-GRANOT-LEAD-LIFECYCLE.md`.
